      "writtenOn": "2026-07-20T14:17:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should actually keep the domain\u0027s refcount elevated as long as the PASID entry exists?\n\nI know we get the domain again in `intel_pasid_setup_first_level()` but this is a TOCTOU? It seems we should get it here instead of `intel_pasid_setup_first_level()` (and in `intel_pasid_setup_first_level()` we should just assign the cache tag)?",
      "revId": "21eb05d165ce6a9df3a6b06e5184ebaf8905773a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "58efe2b5_8db0814c",
        "filename": "drivers/iommu/intel/pkvm/iommu_hc.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 301,
      "author": {
        "id": 3702829
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-20T15:57:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nice catch!\n\nThe refcount we acquire in `intel_pasid_setup_first_level` (`pkvm_get_domain_cache_tag_assign`) stays until the entry is torn down(`pkvm_put_domain_cache_tag_unassign`). So probably keeping the refcount through this function would solve this issue you mentioned? Having the domain refcount elevated through the life time of PASID entry will be taken care of by pkvm_{get,put}_domain_cache_tag_{un}assign? Putting the domain refcount on this function exit would avoid the TOCTOU race. WDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "5f86ef13_958fb647",
      "revId": "21eb05d165ce6a9df3a6b06e5184ebaf8905773a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d89c6557_53255e94",
        "filename": "drivers/iommu/intel/pkvm/iommu_hc.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 301,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-20T17:25:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e So probably keeping the refcount through this function would solve this issue you mentioned?\n\nUgh... Instead of relying on \"overlapping get/put lifetimes\" in a non-obvious hacky way in order to work around our poorly designed hypercall API (wherein the PASID teardown hypercall doesn\u0027t know which domain to get until it finds the PASID entry and parses the `pgd` from it), can\u0027t we just pass the `pgd` value in the PASID teardown hypercall instead? It seems we can: the host\u0027s `pkvm_pasid_teardown()` could easily use `info-\u003edomain-\u003epgd`?\n\nAnd then pKVM could cleanly get the domain _once_ in the PASID setup hypercall and put it _once_ in the PASID teardown hypercall? And `intel_pasid_tear_down_entry()` in pKVM could just assert if the pgd in the PASID entry doesn\u0027t match the passed one?",
      "parentUuid": "58efe2b5_8db0814c",
      "revId": "21eb05d165ce6a9df3a6b06e5184ebaf8905773a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
